          "english": "Run the starter code. Then make a Bank class in which self.accounts = {} is a dict, open_account(self, number, owner, balance=0) makes a new Account and keeps it in the dict, and get_account(self, number) gives back the account from the dict. Then make bank = Bank(), open an account with bank.open_account(2002, \"Rahul\", 2000), take acc2 = bank.get_account(2002), and write print(acc2.deposit(500)). You are done when the output shows two lines: Balance: 1500, Balance: 2500.",
          "hindi": "Starter कोड चलाएँ। फिर एक Bank class बनाएँ जिसमें self.accounts = {} dict हो, open_account(self, number, owner, balance=0) नया Account बना कर dict में रखे, और get_account(self, number) dict से खाता वापस दे। फिर bank = Bank() बनाएँ, bank.open_account(2002, \"Rahul\", 2000) से खाता खोलें, acc2 = bank.get_account(2002) लें, और print(acc2.deposit(500)) लिखें। आप तब सफल हैं जब आउटपुट में दो लाइनें दिखें: Balance: 1500, Balance: 2500।"
