            "hinglish": "Socho aap reverse_string mein text[::-1] ki jagah ek loop likh do: khaali string lo, har letter ko aage jodo. Result wahi hoga — \"python\" se \"nohtyp\" — lekin code lamba hoga aur slow bhi. Interviewer aksar poochta hai: slicing ke bina ulta karke dikhao. Ab socho aap word_frequency mein sentence.split() ki jagah sentence.lower().split() kar do. Ab \"Tea\" aur \"tea\" ek hi gine jayenge — ek chhota badlaav, aur result badal gaya. Ab socho aap second_largest mein sort ki jagah ek hi baar list ko ghum kar largest aur second largest dono nikaal lo. Ye tez hoga, kyunki sort poori list ko arrange karta hai, jabki ek baar ghumne se bhi kaam ho jata hai. Ab socho aap shallow copy ki jagah deep copy use kar lo. Ab andar wali list badalne par asli list nahi badlegi — safe, lekin thoda slow, kyunki har cheez ki nayi copy banti hai. Ab socho aap comprehension ki jagah loop likh do. Result wahi hoga, lekin code 3 lines ka ho jayega.",
