            "english": "In an interview, understanding is tested, not memorising. A list is mutable, a tuple is immutable. *args takes extra values in a tuple, **kwargs takes named values in a dictionary. The GIL is a lock that lets the Python code of only one thread run at a time. A decorator is a function that changes the behaviour of another function. A shallow copy makes only the outer list new, a deep copy makes it new all the way inside. In coding problems, slicing turns a string around, a dictionary counts word frequency, and set plus sort gives the second largest — do not forget to remove duplicates. Prep plan: for the first 3 days, repeat every answer by speaking it and writing it; for the next 3 days, write 2 problems by hand every day; and on the last day, do a mock interview — ask yourself questions and answer out loud. ",
